WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.200
Spider-Man: No Way Home is set to throw&nbsp;
Stephen Strange and Peter Parker into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.000
whole new adventure together — but what's the&nbsp;
comic book background to these two characters'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.920
long-running friendship? This is the untold truth&nbsp;
of Spider-Man and Doctor Strange's relationship.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.360
The first time Spider-Man and Doctor Strange&nbsp;
were shown working together on the printed page&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:27.440
was in 1965's Amazing Spider-Man Annual&nbsp;
#2. This marvelous team-up featured the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.880
webslinger and the Sorcerer Supreme pitting&nbsp;
their wits and powers against a sinister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.240
magic-user named Xandu, who sought to steal a&nbsp;
powerful artifact from the Sanctum Sanctorum.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.640
After foiling the villain's plans in an&nbsp;
interdimensional battle, Strange pledges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.600
his allegiance to Spider-Man, planting the&nbsp;
seed that would grow into a close friendship.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.760
Chronologically, however, Spider-Man&nbsp;
and Strange's first adventure together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.120
may have been much earlier, having been&nbsp;
depicted in 1998's Untold Tales of Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.960
Strange Encounters. In this flashback story,&nbsp;
Strange enlists the wall-crawler's assistance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:08.400
in recovering the mystical Lantern of Lantarr,&nbsp;
which some thugs stole from a museum. Due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.120
an earlier encounter with the lantern-wielding&nbsp;
crooks, Spider-Man's senses have become attuned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:19.200
the ancient object's location. The trail leads to&nbsp;
one of Strange's most dangerous foes, Baron Mordo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.320
who plans to offer human sacrifices to his&nbsp;
patron Enigma in exchange for ultimate power.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.880
In the end, the two heroes defeat Mordo;&nbsp;
Strange subsequently erases the memories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.480
of Mordo's captives at Spider-Man's request, even&nbsp;
though it means they'll forget Spidey's heroics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:40.480
This selfless act makes Strange realize that&nbsp;
there's more to this young man than meets the eye.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.440
Of all the tricks hidden up&nbsp;
Doctor Strange's billowy sleeves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:51.120
his hero-summoning tarot cards are perhaps the&nbsp;
most exciting. When faced with incredible threats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:57.520
that even he can't handle alone, Strange uses his&nbsp;
cards to assemble an impromptu team known as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.640
Secret Defenders. The roster changes depending&nbsp;
on who the cards reveal; more often than not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.720
the selected players are the heroes who are&nbsp;
best equipped to deal with the menace at hand.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.400
In issues #6 to #8 of Secret Defenders,&nbsp;
Strange enlists the aid of Spider-Man and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.600
the Scarlet Witch to stop his persistent&nbsp;
foe Xandu from enacting his latest plan:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:23.360
to merge Earth with the Death Dimension and rule&nbsp;
them both. The cards initially pick Ghost Rider as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.560
the fourth member of the roster, but Strange is&nbsp;
unable to contact him. Instead, Captain America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.760
joins the team, after accidentally stumbling upon&nbsp;
some magical chaos during his nightly patrol.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:39.360
With the aid of the magical Wand of Watoomb,&nbsp;
Xandu nearly succeeds in his plot. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.920
thanks to a last-minute strategy that Strange&nbsp;
and Captain pull off, Xandu's former lover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:49.680
Melinda becomes the queen of the Death Dimension.&nbsp;
Feeling disgust over Xandu's actions, she casts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:54.640
him out of the Death Dimension permanently,&nbsp;
ending his brief but tumultuous reign.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.560
Spider-Man is used to facing all kinds of danger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.840
but even he acknowledges that magical&nbsp;
menaces are a little above his pay grade.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.080
"I mean, I'd rather just stay on&nbsp;
the ground for a little while.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.320
Friendly neighbourhood Spider-Man — someone's&nbsp;
gotta look after the little guy, right?"

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.680
So, whenever these mystical threats&nbsp;
pop up in his corner of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.280
he's more than happy to receive&nbsp;
assistance from the Sorcerer Supreme.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.360
One noteworthy example of this occurred&nbsp;
in the three-part story "Happy Birthday,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:29.680
which ran from Amazing Spider-Man vol.&nbsp;
2 #57 to Amazing Spider-Man vol. 1 #500.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.480
After being soundly defeated and scattered&nbsp;
across various dimensions by Strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.840
the evil being Dormammu tricks New York's&nbsp;
heroes into helping him reconstitute himself.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.360
As swarms of his Mindless Ones overrun Manhattan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:48.800
a mystical mishap knocks Spider-Man and&nbsp;
Doctor Strange outside of time and space.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:54.320
Using a spell, Strange takes Spider-Man through&nbsp;
his whole past up to the exact moment at which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:59.360
all hell broke loose. Spider-Man successfully&nbsp;
prevents the heroes from releasing Dormammu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.240
with only the sorcerer and the web-slinger&nbsp;
having any recollection of what transpired.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.800
As a reward for his help, Strange&nbsp;
hands Spider-Man a tiny golden chest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:13.680
When he opens it, he receives&nbsp;
the best surprise of his life:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.280
A few minutes with his Uncle Ben, who tells him&nbsp;
just how proud he is of the man Peter has become.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.200
During Marvel's Civil War event, Spider-Man does&nbsp;
the unthinkable: In support of the Superhuman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:31.200
Registration Act pioneered by Tony Stark, he&nbsp;
publicly unmasks and tells the world that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.400
is Peter Parker. Unsurprisingly, this&nbsp;
decision proves to be a huge mistake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:41.920
as his Aunt May is hit by a bullet courtesy of&nbsp;
one of the Kingpin's assassins. As the life of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:47.440
his longtime mother figure hangs in the balance,&nbsp;
Peter seeks the aid of Doctor Strange to save her.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:52.080
Unfortunately, Strange admits he can do nothing&nbsp;
to save her life. He helps Peter reach out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.240
the Marvel universe's other geniuses,&nbsp;
but they all give him the same answer:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:01.360
Aunt May is going to die. So, out of pure&nbsp;
desperation, Peter Parker strikes a deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.640
with the demon Mephisto to save his dying&nbsp;
aunt. In return, the demonic ruler asks for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:12.800
Peter's marriage with Mary Jane Watson, which&nbsp;
he deems as the rarest, purest love of all.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:16.560
To hold up his end of the bargain,&nbsp;
Mephisto rewrites history so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.760
the marriage never happened. In this new&nbsp;
reality, Doctor Strange, Mister Fantastic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:27.840
and Iron Man merge science and magic to make&nbsp;
the world forget Spider-Man's secret identity.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.480
In the concluding chapter of "One Moment&nbsp;
in Time," Strange works with Tony Stark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:38.080
and Mister Fantastic to infect the world with a&nbsp;
virus-infused spell, designed to make everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:44.560
forget Spider-Man's secret identity — except for&nbsp;
Peter Parker and Mary Jane Watson. Sound familiar?

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:48.640
"The whole world is about to forget&nbsp;
that Peter Parker is Spider-Man."

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.920
Of course, all of this is rooted&nbsp;
in Peter's deal with Mephisto,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:56.640
but no one, not even Peter himself,&nbsp;
remembers that the demon is involved.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.520
Regardless, this ushers in a "Brand&nbsp;
New Day" for the webslinger, a clean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:06.240
slate of sorts that would remain largely&nbsp;
intact for over a decade in real time.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:12.080
That is, until the events of Amazing Spider-Man&nbsp;
vol. 5 #51 came to pass. In order to free his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.640
spider-powered allies from the thrall of a&nbsp;
literal villain-from-Hell called Kindred,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:21.440
Spider-Man consults Strange, who attempts to&nbsp;
cast a spell with a mystical item to help him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.200
Surprisingly, the spell fails,&nbsp;
prompting Strange to wonder if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:30.400
the wall-crawler has ever unknowingly&nbsp;
struck any mystical deals in the past.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:35.520
Strange's suspicions lead him to the&nbsp;
door of the Hotel Inferno in Las Vegas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:41.600
Mephisto's earthly base of operations. There,&nbsp;
he asks Mephisto point-blank to tell him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:46.080
what's wrong with Peter Parker's soul.&nbsp;
For a while, the infernal lord refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:50.880
give Strange any straight answers, even after&nbsp;
losing a wager with the Sorcerer Supreme over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.960
the outcome of the so-called Sinister&nbsp;
War. Their game continues soon after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.160
however, and Strange eventually manages to put&nbsp;
a stop to Mephisto's plans and free Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:04.880
from the demon's control. Only then is it&nbsp;
revealed why Mephisto targeted Peter and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.920
MJ's relationship in the first place: because&nbsp;
he fears the power of their potential child.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:14.160
Spider-Man and Doctor Strange have&nbsp;
worked together on multiple occasions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.400
showing off their best and worst qualities&nbsp;
to each other in the process. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.480
the good doctor has also had the opportunity&nbsp;
to collaborate with two of the webslinger's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:26.800
most prominent copycats, both of whom&nbsp;
were products of science gone wrong.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:32.720
In the 2017 limited series Damnation, Strange's&nbsp;
longtime ally Wong assembles a temporary team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:38.480
of supernatural heroes to save Las Vegas from&nbsp;
being overtaken by Mephisto's minions. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:44.560
nick of time, the team is saved from certain doom&nbsp;
by the Scarlet Spider, a.k.a. Peter Parker's clone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:50.400
Ben Reilly. Together, they are able to find Doctor&nbsp;
Strange and restore Las Vegas to its normal state.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:55.600
The Sorcerer Supreme has also allied himself&nbsp;
with another superlative-using superhero:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:02.960
the Superior Spider-Man, a reformed Doctor Octopus&nbsp;
occupying a "perfect clone" body of Peter Parker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:09.040
In 2019's Superior Spider-Man vol. 2 #5, the&nbsp;
Eye of Agamotto reveals the true identity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:13.920
the San Francisco-based vigilante to Strange,&nbsp;
after Strange calls for Spider-Man's help.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:19.600
Initially apprehensive to work with a notorious&nbsp;
criminal, Strange and the Superior Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:24.640
set aside their differences and save the day.&nbsp;
Their shared adventure ends with Strange giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:29.280
some well-meaning advice to the arrogant&nbsp;
hero about honesty and accountability.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:34.960
During Spider-Man's brief but memorable time&nbsp;
in his symbiote costume, Peter Parker went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:40.400
on quite a few adventures — some of which he&nbsp;
barely remembers himself. One of these untold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:44.880
chapters of his life was brought to light in&nbsp;
the 2020 limited series Symbiote Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.840
Alien Reality, which also&nbsp;
revealed that at one point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:52.080
he actually received training in the&nbsp;
Mystic Arts from Doctor Strange himself.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:58.320
Waking up to a bizarre world he barely recognizes,&nbsp;
a symbiote-clad Spider-Man rushes to the Sanctum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.440
Sanctorum, hoping to get some clarity from&nbsp;
Strange. What he finds there shocks him:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:08.080
The Hobgoblin, his longtime foe, has&nbsp;
become the apprentice of a different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:12.480
Sorcerer Supreme, and Strange&nbsp;
himself is nowhere to be found.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:18.240
Eventually, the paths of the spider and the true&nbsp;
sorcerer supreme cross, and Strange explains how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.960
the world was transformed by a powerful&nbsp;
book called the Word of God. Together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.440
they concoct a plan to set the world right&nbsp;
again, which includes teaching Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:32.160
a few defensive spells to give him a fighting&nbsp;
chance against his newly mystic-powered foe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:36.880
Strange and Spider-Man manage to defeat&nbsp;
Hobgoblin and his master, Baron Mordo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:41.440
with some assistance from the otherworldly&nbsp;
being called Nightmare. However, Spider-Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:46.560
retains no memory of the events that transpired&nbsp;
— including the spells he learned under Strange.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.560
"Alright, kid. You're an Avenger now."

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:59.440
In his early years, Spider-Man made a number&nbsp;
of attempts to join the Avengers, each with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:04.560
varying levels of success. Prior to 2005,&nbsp;
the closest he had gotten to becoming a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:10.960
card-carrying Avenger was becoming a reserve&nbsp;
member in 1991's Avengers #329. That changed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:16.480
however, when he joined the New Avengers as&nbsp;
a full-time member alongside Captain America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:22.960
Iron Man, Spider-Woman, Luke Cage, Wolverine,&nbsp;
and the Sentry. Not too long after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:28.400
Spider-Man found himself joining hands with&nbsp;
his longtime magical ally, Doctor Strange.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:34.640
New Avengers #27 features the debut of the latest&nbsp;
renegade Avengers team as they rescue their newest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:40.320
recruit, Echo, from Elektra and The Hand. Driven&nbsp;
underground after the events of the superhuman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:46.160
Civil War, this team of new Avengers operates from&nbsp;
Strange's Sanctum Sanctorum, while evading arrest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.160
at the hands of the government-sanctioned&nbsp;
team Avengers led by Iron Man.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:55.760
Once upon a time, whenever Spider-Man and&nbsp;
Doctor Strange teamed up, it was almost a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:00.800
given that their adventures would involve some&nbsp;
form of interdimensional travel. In modern times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.480
however, Spider-Man has found himself&nbsp;
unassisted by the Sorcerer Supreme while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:09.600
crossing the boundaries of the Marvel multiverse&nbsp;
— or, to be more specific, the Spider-Verse.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:15.040
While the concept of a room full of Spider-Men&nbsp;
teaming up was in 1994's Spider-Man: The Animated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.840
Series, the first time that comic books would&nbsp;
adapt the idea on a comparable scale was in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:24.880
2014 multi-part Spider-Verse crossover.&nbsp;
The story features the main Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:30.320
Peter Parker of Earth-616, reaching out to&nbsp;
various Spider-people across time and space&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.520
and enlisting their aid in&nbsp;
a no-holds-barred battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:38.960
against the psychic vampire Morlun. But hey, with&nbsp;
friends like these, who needs Stephen Strange?

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.280
The cooperative relationship between&nbsp;
Spider-Man and Doctor Strange would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:48.720
also be reflected in the dystopian world of&nbsp;
2099 by their future counterparts. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.520
the timely interference of one ends up&nbsp;
saving the other from predestined death.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:12:00.000
The Spider-Man of 2099, Miguel O'Hara, is a gifted&nbsp;
but arrogant geneticist who begins his heroic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.520
journey after a sabotaged lab experiment grants&nbsp;
him spider-powers. Meanwhile, the self-proclaimed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:11.520
Sorceress Supreme of 2099 is a young woman named&nbsp;
Jeannie who trained herself in the Mystic Arts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:19.760
When Spider-Man 2099 and Strange 2099 first meet&nbsp;
in the pages of Spider-Man 2099 #32, the sorceress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:24.960
asks for the aid of the "S-Man" in putting&nbsp;
a stop to a zombie invasion in Mexico City.

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:29.040
After this adventure, the two heroes would&nbsp;
find themselves teaming up from time to time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:32.960
fighting against such foes&nbsp;
as the Maestro, the murderous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:39.280
future version of the Hulk. However, the most&nbsp;
crucial piece of assistance that Spider-Man 2099&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:45.120
ever receives from the Sorceress Supreme happens&nbsp;
in the final issue of his eponymous comic's third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:50.080
volume. Sustaining near-fatal injuries in&nbsp;
a present-day battle against his mutated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.440
hypnotized lover Tempest, Miguel is saved from&nbsp;
certain death by a last-minute spell cast by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.440 --> 00:13:01.040
Strange 2099. By the time Spider-Man 2099 wakes&nbsp;
up, his injuries have been healed, and he has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:06.800
been transported to Strange's headquarters in&nbsp;
the year 2100. It just goes to show — no matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:13.120
where and when they might be, Spider-Man and&nbsp;
Doctor Strange are destined to be best of buds.

